# Design System

When editing shared UI primitives, badges, or visual components:

- **`docs/02-design-system.md`** — visual tone, full status badge catalog (green/amber/blue/red/gray), line-type badges, obligation-type badges, risk badges, severity color tokens, component inventory

## Key rules

1. Use shadcn cards sparingly — subtle border, white/tinted surface, modest rounding, compact spacing.
2. Enterprise tone: dense-but-readable, neutral surfaces, small orange accents for active states only.
3. Status badges use the shared color map in `StatusBadge`. Any new status should extend the catalog, not invent new colors.
4. Icons only when useful. No random illustrations, no marketing-style visuals.
